  {
   "id": "okQJqM5ZCAAJ",
   "from": "Samantha M",
   "author": "eb1bc5d8c49bfec7",
   "date": "2019-01-15T23:25:31Z",
   "subject": "Trap coordinates from discretize()",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve discretized my polygon data to the proximity detector type. Is there a way to get the new xy coordinates for the discretized capture history?</div><div><br></div><div>Using xy(capture_history) works for a non-discretized capture history created using read.capthist(), but this doesn&#39;t work on discretized capture histories, because the new capture history no longer has the xy coordinates, only TrapID. How can I get the spatial locations of the TrapID&#39;s?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "0OTkVLBiCAAJ",
   "from": "Murray Efford",
   "author": "118cea91a1619106",
   "date": "2019-01-16T02:08:17Z",
   "subject": "Re: Trap coordinates from discretize()",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\">I think </span></font></span><code><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"><span>traps</span><span>(</span><span>CH1</span><span>)[</span><span>trap</span><span>(</span><span>CH1</span><span>),]</span></span></font></span><span style=\"color:#660\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif\"> should do it. For example, extending the example for discretize:</span></font></span><b><br></b></span></code></div><div><code><span style=\"color:#660\"><b><br></b></span></code></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>pol </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> make</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">poly</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>CH </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sim</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">capthist</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">pol</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> popn </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">30</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> detectpar </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g0 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>CH1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> discretize</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> spacing </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> output </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;count&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>cbind</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">animalID</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> occasion</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> traps</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">trap</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),])</span></div></code></div><br>See also the plot at the end of Examples.</div><div><br></div><div>Murray<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br>On Wednesday, January 16, 2019 at 12:25:31 PM UTC+13, Samantha M wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve discretized my polygon data to the proximity detector type. Is there a way to get the new xy coordinates for the discretized capture history?</div><div><br></div><div>Using xy(capture_history) works for a non-discretized capture history created using read.capthist(), but this doesn&#39;t work on discretized capture histories, because the new capture history no longer has the xy coordinates, only TrapID. How can I get the spatial locations of the TrapID&#39;s?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you</div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
