lor:#066\">30</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> detectpar </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g0 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.3</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>CH1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> discretize</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> spacing </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">10</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> output </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;count&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>cbind</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">animalID</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> occasion</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> traps</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)[</span><span style=\"color:#000\">trap</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">CH1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),])</span></div></code></div><br>See also the plot at the end of Examples.</div><div><br></div><div>Murray<br></div><br>On Wednesday, January 16, 2019 at 12:25:31 PM UTC+13, Samantha M wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div><br></div><div>I&#39;ve discretized my polygon data to the proximity detector type. Is there a way to get the new xy coordinates for the discretized capture history?</div><div><br></div><div>Using xy(capture_history) works for a non-discretized capture history created using read.capthist(), but this doesn&#39;t work on discretized capture histories, because the new capture history no longer has the xy coordinates, only TrapID. How can I get the spatial locations of the TrapID&#39;s?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you</div></div></blockquote></div></blockquote></div>"
